# gr2 `review run` install hint: read when --install is omitted.
#
# grip's importable Python package lives in the gr2/ subdir, and its test runner
# (pytest) is declared in the gr2 `[dev]` optional-dependency, so a plain
# `pip install -e <lane>` at the repo root cannot install it. Declaring it here
# lets a reviewer run `gr2 review run <lane>` on a grip lane with no hand-written
# --install/--package.
#
# {venv} = the lane venv's python; {lane} = the lane (repo root). The line is
# shell-split first, then {venv}/{lane} substituted per token (so a lane path with
# a space stays one token).
install = {venv} -m pip install -e {lane}/gr2[dev]
package = gr2_overlay
